## 4. C++ (C++17+)

```cpp
#include <fstream>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::ifstream file("myfile.txt");
    std::vector<std::string> lines;
    std::string line;

    while (std::getline(file, line)) {
        lines.push_back(line);   // line does NOT contain '\n'
    }

    // Process
    for (const auto& l : lines) {
        std::cout << l << '\n';
    }
}
```

*Tip:* If you only need to process each line, keep the loop and avoid storing all lines.

